<title>PAKISTAN: Pakistan State Oil falls 0.97 percent.</title>
<headline>Pakistan State Oil falls 0.97 percent.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-05-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>State-run Pakistan State Oil (PSO) stock fell three rupees, or 0.97 percent, to 307 on Tuesday, settlement day at the Karachi stock exchange, amid profit-taking, dealers said.</p>
<p>PSO has already paid a 30 percent interim cash dividend for the year ending June 30.</p>
<p>PSO's 10-rupee stock rose to 325 after PSO its first-half results in March, which showed a 58 percent rise in after-tax profit to 869 million rupees from 548 million in the year-ago period.</p>
<p>($1 = 40.43 rupees) -- Ibrahim Khan 9221-5685192.</p>
